# API Organization

The API modules in this project follow a domain-driven organization pattern, mirroring the business domains in the application.

## API Structure

- API modules are located in [src/api/](mdc:src/api/) and divided by business domain
- Each domain has its own directory (e.g., system, crm, erp, mall, pay, etc.)
- Each API module typically exports functions that make HTTP requests to the backend

## Common API Patterns

- API functions use the axios HTTP client, configured in [src/utils/request.ts](mdc:src/utils/request.ts)
- API endpoints follow RESTful conventions where possible
- Pagination, sorting, and filtering follow consistent patterns across modules
- Each domain directory contains modules for different entities within that domain

## API Usage Example

```typescript
// Import an API module
import { getList, getDetail, create, update, remove } from '@/api/system/user'

// Using the API in a component
const loadUsers = async () => {
  const { list, total } = await getList(queryParams)
  userData.value = list
  totalCount.value = total
}
```

When adding new API endpoints, follow the existing patterns in similar modules to maintain consistency throughout the codebase.
